  "body": "Well, https://tc39.es/ecma262/multipage/ecmascript-data-types-and-values.html#sec-ecmascript-language-types-string-type does define empty string, and it is pretty obvious, but Infra itself doesn't have a link for empty string.\r\n\r\n(Unless strings are considered as lists somehow. (I don't think they are, even though strings are finite ordered sequences.))\r\n\r\n(Edit: \"empty list\" is defined by \"list is empty\", though it doesn't automatically link)",
